==== 1. Force law F = c i^2 exp(-x/lam), refitted from the hover visits ====
  42 visits (18 morning + 24 afternoon, rocking-flagged visits excluded)
  lam = 5.905 mm  (95 % CI +-4.3 %)
  c   = 3.294 / 3.023 N/A^2 for 39 / 42 g  (95 % CI +-7.4 / +-7.4 %; correlation with lam -1.00)
  residual: 5.9 mA rms, max 14.4 mA
  95 % CI of the predicted hover current, 9-11 mm: +-0.57 % (39 g) / +-0.50 % (42 g) at worst
PASS: refit reproduces the s08 values exactly (lam, c_39, c_42)
PASS: the +-5 % range used for lam covers its 95 % CI (+-4.3 %)
  NOTE: c alone is poorly determined (CI +-7.4 %) because it is strongly correlated with lam (-1.00).
        What the linear model needs is the hover current i0 at the operating gap, and that is known to
        +-0.57 %. Section 6 therefore checks the uncertainty set against the measured currents directly.

